{
  "version": "0.9.2",
  "notes": "gps_test.py (0.9.1) crashed on real hardware: 'TypeError: unexpected keyword argument on_progress' -- it called Gps.read()'s brand new on_progress parameter, but the device's ALREADY-INSTALLED gps.py (from before this OTA) didn't have it yet. Real bug: a diagnostic test script should never require a firmware change just to run -- pasting a test script directly into Thonny (a completely normal, expected way to use these bench tests) doesn't go through OTA first. Fixed: gps_test.py is now fully self-contained, calling ONLY Gps.on()/off()/read(timeout_s, poll_interval_s) -- the exact signature that has existed since gps.py was first created -- in repeated short 5s chunks instead of depending on a new callback parameter. Reverted Gps.read()'s on_progress addition entirely (gps.py is back to byte-for-byte its pre-0.9.1 self) since nothing needs it anymore.",
